  "articleBody": "It's a common dilemma: you have a repair or a small project, and you're wondering if you need a handyman or a specialized, licensed contractor. Generally, handyman services are perfect for those smaller, non-structural tasks that don't involve significant changes to permitted systems. Think leaky faucets, drywall repair, hanging shelves, or patching a hole. They're your go-to for a wide breadth of tasks that keep your home running smoothly without needing specialized licenses. However, if your project involves electrical wiring, plumbing beyond a simple fixture replacement, significant structural changes, or HVAC work, you're likely entering licensed contractor territory. These types of jobs often require specific permits and adherence to complex building codes to ensure safety and compliance. A frequent mistake is assuming a handyman can handle work that truly requires a licensed specialist. While a good handyman can do a lot, knowing the line is crucial. If the work changes permitted systems, requires detailed plans, or involves significant safety considerations, a licensed or specialized professional becomes important. HH Remodeling LLC offers both handyman services and can act as a general contractor for larger projects, so we can help you determine the right approach.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}